{
  "_help": [
    "Write words lowercase, without accents (Greek too: προυπολογισμ, not προϋπολογισμ). Serbian/Russian Cyrillic is turned into Latin first, so 'budzet' also finds 'буџет'.",
    "A plain word matches the START of a word, so one entry covers all endings: 'biudzet' finds biudžetas, biudžetą, biudžeto, biudžetui, biudžetus, biudžetai.",
    "'word$' matches only that exact word; used for short words that would otherwise hit other words ('alga$' must not find 'algoritmas'), so every form is listed.",
    "'~word' matches anywhere inside a word (Hebrew, where ה/ב/ל/ו/ש are glued to the front).",
    "'+word' counts only when the same sentence also has a sum of money - for words that often mean something else ('bilancio' = win/loss record, 'uždirbo 20 taškų' = scored 20 points, 'earned the win').",
    "'salary_ignore_phrases' are cut out of a sentence before salary words are looked for: 'l'ingaggio di Kevin Knox' (= the signing of) is ignored, 'un ingaggio importante' (= a big salary) still counts.",
    "'ignore_sentences_with': a sentence with one of these words is skipped completely (fantasy games talk about a 'budget' and player prices).",
    "'ignore_money_in_sentences_with': in a sentence about fines or tickets, sums of money don't count; budget/salary words still do ('ticket income is 20% of the budget' is kept, 'tickets from 10 euros' is not).",
    "budget -> Budget label, salary -> Salary label, money -> Amount label (sums of money: currencies, million/thousand words, and € $ £ ₪ next to a number are found automatically)."
  ],
